  * ChunkIsRtl --
  *
  *	Determine if a string of UTF-8 text has RTL base direction, by
- *	scanning for the first Unicode character with a strong bidi category.
- *	RTL strong categories: R (Arabic Letter excluded), AL, RLE, RLO, RLI.
- *	LTR strong categories: L, LRE, LRO, LRI.
+ *	scanning for the first Unicode character with a strong bidi class.
  *	This is the Unicode P2/P3 paragraph-direction algorithm applied at
  *	chunk level, which is sufficient for the single-script chunks that
  *	TkTextCharLayoutProc produces.
  *
+ *	The Bidi_Class of every character is taken from the mojibake
+ *	Unicode tables (Unicode 18) that Tk already ships, so no code-point
+ *	ranges are hand-maintained here.  Per UAX #9 only the strong classes
+ *	L, R and AL decide the direction: in particular non-spacing marks
+ *	(NSM) are skipped, and rule W1 resolves them to the class of the
+ *	preceding character (to the embedding level at the start of text).
+ *	This makes a base-less vowel point such as an orphan Hebrew nikkud
+ *	(U+05B0) neutral, instead of letting it flip the direction of a
+ *	whole chunk that actually starts with strong LTR text. [8504cdc7c8]
+ *
  * Results:
  *	true if the chunk is RTL, false if LTR or neutral.
  */
